# Mock Page Data Rules

> **Maintenance**: Update this file when page JSON shape, naming, templates, or adapter matching changes (`rules-sync.mdc`).

## Page JSON structure

Mock page JSON files **mirror the Strapi API response shape** so `MockAdapter` and `StrapiAdapter` use the same `toPageData` / `toNavigationData` transform pipeline. Both adapters pass raw JSON through `strapi-document.ts` functions.

```json
{
  "slug": "/about",
  "lang": "en",
  "template": "default",
  "seo": {
    "title": "Page Title",
    "description": "Meta description",
    "ogImage": "https://..."
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "__component": "blocks.hero",
      "id": 1,
      "headline": "...",
      "cta": { "__component": "shared.cta-link", "id": 2, "label": "...", "href": "..." }
    }
  ]
}
```

Key differences from the old format:
- `lang` (not `locale`) — Strapi i18n reserves `locale`.
- Blocks use `__component` + numeric `id` (Strapi dynamic zone shape) — **not** `{ type, props }`.
- Fields are flat on the block object — no `props` wrapper.
- Nested components also carry `__component` + `id`.

`strapi-document.ts → toDynamicZoneBlock` strips `__component`/`id` and produces `BlockInstance { id, type, props }` for the renderer.

## Block IDs

Numeric integers, unique within the page. Prefer sequential numbering (1, 2, 3, …).

## Templates

| Value | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `default` | Header + footer (standard pages) |
| `detail` | Header + footer + two-column main (resort) |
| `bare` | No header/footer |

Must match a file in `src/tenants/{tenant}/templates/{name}.tsx`.

## Dynamic route pages

For slugs with params (e.g. `/rooms/:roomId`), set `slugPattern` and use `:` segments:

```json
{
  "slug": "/rooms/:roomId",
  "slugPattern": "/rooms/:roomId",
  "template": "default",
  "blocks": []
}
```

`MockAdapter` scans all `pages/*.json` and matches `slugPattern` (or `slug` if it contains `:`) via regex — no separate `patternFiles` list.

## File naming

- Home: `home.json` (slug `/`)
- Static: `{segment}.json` or nested `rooms--all.json` for `/rooms/all`
- Localized override: `{locale}--{path}.json` (e.g. `de--about.json`) — tried before fallback `about.json`
- Pattern pages: descriptive name (e.g. `room-detail.json`)

## Block `__component`

Must be `"blocks.{type}"` matching a Strapi component and a key in `registerTenantBlocks()` or `registerSharedBlocks()`.

## Collections

Collection files live at `src/core/mock-data.ts/{tenant}/collections/{name}.json`. They are loaded by `MockAdapter.getCollection`. Items must have a `slug` field (used by `MockAdapter.getEntry` to look up a single item — it matches `item.slug === id || item.id === id`).

Structure (e.g. `collections/products.json`):
```json
[
  { "slug": "merida", "name": "Merida Road Ride", "price": 350, ... }
]
```

Locale-specific overrides: `{locale}--{name}.json` (e.g. `en--products.json`).

## After editing mock pages

Update `mock-data-pages.mdc` and the tenant `catalog.mdc` when behavior changes (see `rules-sync.mdc`).

Mock folder vs tenant id: see `scripts/tenant-mock-map.json` (e.g. `resort-example` → `src/core/mock-data.ts/resort/`).
